  "name": "HIV P24 ANTIGEN DETECTION",
  "code": "2772",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Remarks :&nbsp;</span></strong><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">1.&nbsp;HIV - DUO determines the presence of HIV p24 antigen and antibodies to HIV -1 group and HIV-2.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">2.&nbsp;It is a screening test. All Reactive results are crosschecked by immunochromatography method and ELFA, reported as per NACO guidelines.</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">3.&nbsp;All Reactive results need to be confirmed by alternate methods, like Western Blot.</span><br><strong><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Abbreviation :</span></strong><br><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\"><strong>CMIA : </strong>Chemiluminescence Microparticle Immunoassay</span></p>",
